  "cards": [
    {
      "dot": "cyan",
      "title": "Listener journey",
      "items": [
        "A single AudioProvider stays mounted above consumer navigation. Audio goes straight to the selected stream.",
        "Home renders four advertisement slots and a pausable announcement ticker. Both poll while the page is visible.",
        "Android bundles the web app, routes API requests to the configured server and uses native media-session controls."
      ]
    },
    {
      "dot": "rose",
      "title": "Publication and trust",
      "items": [
        "With accounts configured, staff access the workspace; only managers and administrators may publish. The server rechecks the session and role.",
        "Supabase RLS and column grants enforce account ownership and content publishing. Writes use the caller token, not a service-role secret.",
        "With accounts off, publishing accepts only loopback requests and stores JSON on the server. Browser drafts remain distinct."
      ]
    },
    {
      "dot": "amber",
      "title": "Implementation boundaries",
      "items": [
        "The server proxies live metadata, not continuous listener audio. Centova administration is not connected.",
        "Six additional stations, schedules, analytics and many admin operations remain illustrative or local drafts.",
        "Default live audio is plain HTTP. TLS at the stream, deployed migrations and Android device reliability are deployment checks, not proven by this source map."
      ]
    },
    {
      "dot": "slate",
      "title": "Evidence snapshot",
      "items": [
        "Source evidence is pinned to ec66b05. No environment files, credentials, local drafts or generated APKs were read into this map.",
        "The listener navigation rails are temporarily hidden. Legacy browser tests still assume those rails exist.",
        "This analysis describes source behavior; it does not certify the running database, hosting configuration or all native-device behavior."
      ]
    }
  ]
